Changed: IBTK::FACPreconditionerStrategy has the new virtual functions reinitializeOperatorState(), getLayoutKeySpecialized(), and initializeOperatorCoefficientsSpecialized(). When IBTK::FACPreconditioner::initializeSolverState() initializes a preconditioner that is already initialized, it calls reinitializeOperatorState() instead of deallocateOperatorState() and initializeOperatorState(). In that case, the preconditioner no longer calls its virtual deallocateSolverState(). The Poisson FAC operators (see the entry on improved FAC re-initialization) reuse their layout when the hierarchy, the vectors, and getLayoutKeySpecialized() are unchanged. In that case, they call initializeOperatorCoefficientsSpecialized() instead of initializeOperatorStateSpecialized(). If the initializeOperatorStateSpecialized() override of a subclass of one of these operators builds state that depends on the coefficients or the boundary conditions, the subclass must either override initializeOperatorCoefficientsSpecialized() and call the base function, or override getLayoutKeySpecialized() to return false. Returning false makes every initialization a full one. The same applies to state that its smoothError() or computeResidual() override reads. Direct subclasses of IBTK::PoissonFACPreconditionerStrategy, and IBAMR::StaggeredStokesFACPreconditionerStrategy and its subclasses, see no change. The Poisson FAC operators now re-initialize their coarse and level solvers without deallocating them. This relies on the contract of IBTK::GeneralSolver::initializeSolverState(): a solver that returns early when it is already initialized uses stale coefficients. The new virtual functions change the vtables of these classes.
